# .gitignore for viromelib-local  —  ~/Desktop/viromelib/.gitignore
# Revised 2026-10-26. Goal: track code, notebooks and documentation; ignore data, large
# binaries and regenerable figure output.
#
# USE ONE IGNORE FILE, AT THE REPO ROOT. Delete ~/Desktop/viromelib/flaviLib/.gitignore.
# That nested file ignored `figures/`, which inside flaviLib/ means flaviLib/figures/**, so
# every flaviLib notebook was being ignored. Two ignore files with different rules is how that
# went unnoticed; this file covers both trees.
#
# WHY THERE IS NO `!*.Rmd` RESCUE BLOCK HERE. The old file ended with `!*.Rmd`, `!*.R`, `!*.py`,
# `!*.md`, `!*.cm` and friends. Those were no-ops: nothing above them excluded those extensions,
# so they rescued nothing. Worse, they read as though notebooks were protected by an explicit
# rule when they were only tracked because no pattern happened to catch them. Nothing below
# excludes source files, so nothing needs rescuing.
#
# AND THE RULE THAT CAUSED THE FLAVILIB BUG: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so once `figures/` is ignored you CANNOT re-include anything inside it — `!figures/**/*.Rmd`
# has no effect, because the files are unreachable rather than merely overridden. Exclude the
# CONTENTS, never the directory, whenever you want to keep some files from inside it.

# ── System and editor junk
.DS_Store
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
~$*

# ── Whole trees that are data, not source
data/
work/
libraryDesign/
outputs-sequencefiles/
trash/

# ── Figure inputs and outputs, at ANY depth in EITHER tree.
# Pattern-based rather than enumerated, so it keeps working as figure directories are added
# or renamed. The old file named figures/fig1/inputs and figures/fig1/plots explicitly, which
# stopped covering anything once rank/, representation/, ncbi_virus_space/ and igv/ appeared.
# Directories themselves stay walkable so notebooks beside them remain trackable.
**/inputs/**
**/plots/**
!**/inputs/
!**/plots/
!**/inputs/**/*.md5
!**/plots/**/*.md5
# A figure input manifest IS worth tracking: a clone cannot knit without the inputs, so at
# minimum it should be able to say exactly which files it is missing.

# ── R Markdown / htmlwidgets GENERATED output. Added 2026-10-26 after plotly, jQuery,
# crosstalk and typedarray bundles (~30 files, most of a 1.4 MiB push) were committed from
# figures/rank/20261019/rank_all_files/. knitr writes a `<name>_files/` directory beside any
# non-self-contained HTML output and regenerates it on every knit.
# NOTE this is also why a knit must write into plots/<date>_<strategy>/ -- that output went to
# figures/rank/20261019/ instead, so the **/plots/** rules never applied to it.
*_files/
*_cache/
*.js
*.css
*.scss
*.map
*.igv_batch
*.igv_session.xml

# ── Tabular data and rendered output, globally. All regenerable from a notebook plus inputs.
# NOTE *.txt is global, so plain-text documentation disappears silently. Keep documentation
# in Markdown — *.md is deliberately not ignored anywhere in this file.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.txt
*.tbl
*.json
*.xml
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.html
*.nb.html
*.pdf
*.svg
*.png
*.tiff
*.tif
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.eps
*.ai

# ── Sequence, alignment and interval files
*.fa
*.fasta
*.fa.fai
*.fa.ssi
*.fai
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.bam
*.bam.bai
*.bai
*.sam
*.cram
*.bed
*.gtf
*.bedGraph
*.bw
*.bigWig

# ── Archives and serialised data (these were the real gap: none of the extensions above
# catches an .rds or a .parquet, so they would have been committed silently)
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.gz
*.rds
*.RDS
*.feather
*.parquet
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.npy
*.npz

# ── Kept deliberately: covariance models and alignments are small, versioned inputs that
# define the CM vocabulary (decision 25), so they are NOT ignored above. Listed here only so
# the omission reads as a choice rather than an oversight: *.cm, *.stk, *.sto.
